Patch summary:
Keep the pulled-down shade's clock and status icons where the status bar's
are. The header takes the status bar's paddings (its content insets, then
status_bar_padding_start at the start; status_bar_padding_end and the icons'
end padding at the end) instead of its own 16dp to 40dp, and its clock the
status bar clock's start padding (status_bar_clock_starting_padding) instead
of 0dp. They are applied again at every inset, configuration and resource
change, once more after a configuration change, and when the status bar's
content insets change: read during a change, the insets could still be the
old ones. The header's own values put the clock and icons elsewhere, by an
amount that changed with the layout and as the screen was resized. A mouse
click on the header's status icons closes the shade, as one on the status
bar's opened it in the same place; the narrow layout's header ignored it.
Ika's System UI overlay makes the header as tall as the status bar.

